# agent-orchestrator commit message template (issue #5).
# Enable with:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
# Lines starting with '#' are stripped from the final message.
#
# EVERY COMMIT REFERENCES ITS ISSUE (AGENTS.md golden rule 1 / GR-2). The
# trailer layout is a POSITION RULE, NOT A PRESENCE RULE: the layout below is
# the one scripts/check-pr-contract.sh (issue #288) actually enforces, quoted
# from that script's own parser:
#
#   * The ticket reference is `Refs kushin77/agent-orchestrator#<n>`, on its own
#     line, in the TRAILING TRAILER BLOCK: the last paragraph(s) whose every
#     line is a `Token: value` line, a continuation line, or the reference line
#     itself. A `Token: value` line matches `^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*:[ \t]*\S`.
#   * The reference itself is matched by the python regex
#     `Refs:?\s+[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+#[0-9]+`, so this repo's
#     colon-less form (above) and git's own colon form (`Refs: kushin77/...`)
#     are both accepted. `git interpret-trailers --parse` alone would refuse the
#     colon-less form — it recognises only the colon form — which is why the
#     block is parsed by position instead.
#   * A mention in the SUBJECT IS NOT A TRAILER. The three refusals, by name:
#     `commit-ref-only-in-subject` (in the subject only),
#     `commit-ref-outside-the-trailer-block` (in a prose paragraph only), and
#     `commit-missing-ticket-trailer` (no reference at all). A bare substring
#     test accepts the first two, which is exactly the defect (#287) that this
#     position rule closes.
#   * A bare `---------` line is the separator GitHub inserts when it composes a
#     squash-merge message. It is transparent to the walk-back — the trailing
#     block continues past it — and prose is not (issue #522).
#   * Keep numeric references out of these `#` comment lines. git strips them
#     only under the default `strip` cleanup (the editor path); under
#     `git commit -F` / `--cleanup=whitespace` a surviving comment is prose, and
#     a numeric reference inside it is refused as
#     `commit-ref-outside-the-trailer-block`. The `<issue>` / `<n>` placeholders
#     below are chosen so they can never match.
#
# THE PR BODY carries the rest of the contract (checked at PR time — the PR body
# is read, not the commit message):
#   * `Closes #<n>` on its own line (`^Closes[[:space:]]+#[0-9]+`);
#   * a FILLED-IN `AI-assistance: <runtime> (<mode>)` line, matched as
#     `^AI-assistance:[[:space:]]*[^<[:space:]][^(]*\([^)]*\)[[:space:]]*$` —
#     the `<runtime>` placeholder is refused, so an untouched template can never
#     pass as a declaration;
#   * a `## Pre-existing red` section holding either an explicit `None` or a
#     `Reproduce:` line naming a command in backticks, followed by a fenced
#     output block.
#
# Measured 2026-09-14: `git config commit.template` is unset on this machine
# (rc 1), so this file is advisory until you enable it with the command above.

<type>(<scope>): <short summary>
# imperative, <= 72 chars. Types: feat / fix / refactor / docs / chore / test.
# Example:  feat(foundation): add repo scaffold + agent-instruction layering

<why: motivation / context>
<what: the change>

Refs kushin77/agent-orchestrator#<issue>
AI-assistance: <runtime> (<mode>)
